"Claude Platform release notes - Claude Platform Docs (https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/release-notes/overview)\nciteturn31567view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn31565view0\",\"lineno\":600}); Total lines: 901\nL568: ### January 23rd, 2025\nL569: \nL570:   * We've launched citations capability in the API, allowing Claude to provide source attribution for information. Learn more in cite242†Citations .\nL571:   * We've added support for plain text documents and custom content documents in the Messages API.\nL572: \nL573: ### January 21st, 2025\nL574: \nL575:   * We announced the deprecation of the Claude 2, Claude 2.1, and Claude Sonnet 3 models. Read more in cite39†Model deprecations .\nL576: ### January 15th, 2025\nL577: \nL578:   * We've updated cite162†prompt caching to be easier to use. Now, when you set a cache breakpoint, we'll automatically read from your longest previously cached prefix.\nL579:   * You can now put words in Claude's mouth when using tools.\nL580: \nL581: ### January 10th, 2025\nL582: \nL583:   * We've optimized support for cite243†prompt caching in the Message Batches API to improve cache hit rate.\nL584: \nL585: ### December 19th, 2024\nL586: \nL587:   * We've added support for a cite244†delete endpoint in the Message Batches API.\nL588: ### December 17th, 2024\nL589: \nL590: The following features are now available in the Claude API without a beta header:\nL591:   * cite34†Models API : Query available models, validate model IDs, and resolve cite5†model aliases to their canonical model IDs.\nL592:   * cite245†Message Batches API : Process large batches of messages asynchronously at 50% of the standard API cost.\nL593:   * cite246†Token counting API : Calculate token counts for Messages before sending them to Claude.\nL594:   * cite162†Prompt Caching : Reduce costs by up to 90% and latency by up to 80% by caching and reusing prompt content.\nL595:   * cite237†PDF support : Process PDFs to analyze both text and visual content within documents.\nL596: We also released new official SDKs:\nL597: \nL598:   * cite235†Java SDK†github.com (alpha)\nL599:   * cite233†Go SDK†github.com (alpha)\nL600: ### December 4th, 2024\nL601: \nL602:   * We've added the ability to group by API key on the cite217†Usage†console.anthropic.com and cite227†Cost†console.anthropic.com pages of the cite209†Developer Console†console.anthropic.com .\nL603:   * We've added two new Last used at and Cost columns and the ability to sort by any column on the cite247†API keys†console.anthropic.com page of the cite209†Developer Console†console.anthropic.com .\nL604: ### November 21st, 2024\nL605: \nL606:   * We've released the cite3†Admin API , allowing users to programmatically manage their organization's resources.\nL607: \nL608: ### November 20th, 2024\nL609: \nL610:   * We've updated our rate limits for the Messages API. We've replaced the tokens per minute rate limit with new input and output tokens per minute rate limits. Read more in cite139†Rate limits .\nL611:   * We've added support for cite240†tool use in the cite241†Workbench†console.anthropic.com .\nL612: ### November 13th, 2024\nL613: \nL614:   * We've added PDF support for all Claude Sonnet 3.5 models. Read more in cite237†PDF support .\nL615: \nL616: ### November 6th, 2024\nL617: \nL618:   * We've retired the Claude 1 and Instant models. Read more in cite39†Model deprecations .\nL619: \nL620: ### November 4th, 2024\nL621: \nL622:   * cite248†Claude Haiku 3.5†www.anthropic.com is now available on the Claude API as a text-only model.\nL623: ### November 1st, 2024\nL624: \nL625:   * We've added PDF support for use with the new Claude Sonnet 3.5. Read more in cite237†PDF support .\nL626:   * We've also added token counting, which allows you to determine the total number of tokens in a Message prior to sending it to Claude. Read more in cite246†Token counting .\nL627: ### October 22nd, 2024\nL628: \nL629:   * We've added Anthropic-defined computer use tools to our API for use with the new Claude Sonnet 3.5. Read more in cite28†Computer use tool .\nL630:   * Claude Sonnet 3.5, our most intelligent model yet, just got an upgrade and is now available on the Claude API. Read more in the cite249†Claude Sonnet documentation†www.anthropic.com .\nL631: ### October 8th, 2024\nL632:   * The Message Batches API is now available in beta. Process large batches of queries asynchronously in the Claude API for 50% less cost. Read more in cite245†Batch processing .\nL633:   * We've loosened restrictions on the ordering of `user`/`assistant` turns in our Messages API. Consecutive `user`/`assistant` messages will be combined into a single message instead of erroring, and we no longer require the first input message to be a `user` message.\nL634:   * We've deprecated the Build and Scale plans in favor of a standard feature suite (formerly referred to as Build), along with additional features that are available through sales. Read more in our cite250†API pricing information†claude.com .\nL635: ### October 3rd, 2024\nL636: \nL637:   * We've added the ability to disable parallel tool use in the API. Set `disable_parallel_tool_use: true` in the `tool_choice` field to ensure that Claude uses at most one tool. Read more in cite251†Parallel tool use .\nL638: ### September 10th, 2024\nL639: \nL640:   * We've added Workspaces to the cite209†Developer Console†console.anthropic.com . Workspaces allow you to set custom spend or rate limits, group API keys, track usage by project, and control access with user roles. Read more in our cite252†blog post†www.anthropic.com .\nL641: \nL642: ### September 4th, 2024\nL643: \nL644:   * We announced the deprecation of the Claude 1 models. Read more in cite39†Model deprecations .\nL645: ### August 22nd, 2024\nL646: \nL647:   * We've added support for usage of the SDK in browsers by returning CORS headers in the API responses. Set `dangerouslyAllowBrowser: true` in the SDK instantiation to enable this feature.\nL648: \nL649: ### August 19th, 2024\nL650: \nL651:   * 8,192-token outputs on Claude Sonnet 3.5 are out of beta and no longer require the `max-tokens-3-5-sonnet-2024-07-15` header.\nL652: ### August 14th, 2024\nL653: \nL654:   * cite162†Prompt caching is now available as a beta feature in the Claude API. Cache and re-use prompts to reduce latency by up to 80% and costs by up to 90%.\nL655: \nL656: ### July 15th, 2024\nL657: \nL658:   * Generate outputs up to 8,192 tokens in length from Claude Sonnet 3.5 with the new `anthropic-beta: max-tokens-3-5-sonnet-2024-07-15` header.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nComputation and Language Feb 2026 (https://arxiv.org/list/cs.CL/2026-02?show=100&skip=400)\nciteturn31567view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn31565view4\",\"lineno\":355}); Total lines: 933\nL307: Title: Uncovering Cross-Objective Interference in Multi-Objective Alignment\nL308: \nL309: cite343†Yining Lu , cite344†Meng Jiang L310: \nL311: Subjects: Computation and Language (cs.CL); Machine Learning (cs.LG)\nL312: \nL313: [435] cite345†arXiv:2602.06920 [cite346†pdf , cite347†html , cite348†other ]\nL314: \nL315: \nL316: Title: Halluverse-M^3: A multitask multilingual benchmark for hallucination in LLMs\nL317: \nL318: cite349†Samir Abdaljalil , cite350†Parichit Sharma , cite351†Erchin Serpedin , cite352†Hasan Kurban L319: \nL320: Subjects: Computation and Language (cs.CL); Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)\nL321: [436] cite353†arXiv:2602.06942 [cite354†pdf , cite355†html , cite356†other ]\nL322: \nL323: \nL324: Title: Optimal Turkish Subword Strategies at Scale: Systematic Evaluation of Data, Vocabulary, Morphology Interplay\nL325: \nL326: cite357†Duygu Altinok L327: \nL3