uz Madahian L434: \nL435: Comments: EACL 2026\nL436: Subjects: Computation and Language (cs.CL); Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)\nL437: \nL438: [448] cite462†arXiv:2602.07211 [cite463†pdf , cite464†html , cite465†other ]\nL439: \nL440: \nL441: Title: Equipping LLM with Directional Multi-Talker Speech Understanding Capabilities\nL442: \nL443: cite466†Ju Lin , cite467†Jing Pan , cite468†Ruizhi Li , cite469†Ming Sun , cite27†Yuzong Liu , cite470†Alaa Hassan , cite471†Jing Zheng , cite472†Florian Metze L444: \nL445: Subjects: Computation and Language (cs.CL); Sound (cs.SD)\nL446: \nL447: [449] cite473†arXiv:2602.07319 [cite474†pdf , cite475†html , cite476†other ]\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2602.07306v1] Parallel Track Transformers: Enabling Fast GPU Inference with Reduced Synchronization (https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.07306v1)\nciteturn31567view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn31566view4\",\"lineno\":16}); Total lines: 160\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Distributed, Parallel, and Cluster Computing\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 7 Feb 2026]\nL9: # Title:Parallel Track Transformers: Enabling Fast GPU Inference with Reduced Synchronization\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Chong Wang , cite6†Nan Du , cite7†Tom Gunter , cite8†Tao Lei , cite9†Kulin Seth , cite10†Senyu Tong , cite11†Jianyu Wang , cite12†Guoli Yin , cite13†Xiyou Zhou , cite14†Kelvin Zou , cite15†Ruoming Pang L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Parallel Track Transformers: Enabling Fast GPU Inference with Reduced Synchronization, by Chong Wang and 10 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite16†View PDF cite17†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Efficient large-scale inference of transformer-based large language models (LLMs) remains a fundamental systems challenge, frequently requiring multi-GPU parallelism to meet stringent latency and throughput targets. Conventional tensor parallelism decomposes matrix operations across devices but introduces substantial inter-GPU synchronization, leading to communication bottlenecks and degraded scalability.\nL17: We propose the Parallel Track (PT) Transformer, a novel architectural paradigm that restructures computation to minimize cross-device dependencies. PT achieves up to a 16x reduction in synchronization operations relative to standard tensor parallelism, while maintaining competitive model quality in our experiments.\nL18: We integrate PT into two widely adopted LLM serving stacks-Tensor-RT-LLM and vLLM-and report consistent improvements in serving efficiency, including up to 15-30% reduced time to first token, 2-12% reduced time per output token, and up to 31.90% increased throughput in both settings.\nL19: Subjects:  | Distributed, Parallel, and Cluster Computing (cs.DC); Machine Learning (cs.LG)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite18†arXiv:2602.07306 [cs.DC]\nL21:    | (or cite19†arXiv:2602.07306v1 [cs.DC] for this version)\nL22:    | cite20†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2602.07306†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Chong Wang [cite21†view email ]\nL26: [v1] Sat, 7 Feb 2026 01:42:20 UTC (57 KB)\nL27: \nL28: Full-text links:\nL29: \nL30: ## Access Paper:\nL31: \nL32: View a PDF of the paper titled Parallel Track Transformers: Enabling Fast GPU Inference with Reduced Synchronization, by Chong Wang and 10 other authors\nL33: \nL34:   * cite16†View PDF L35:   * cite17†HTML (experimental) L36:   * cite22†TeX Source L37: \nL38: cite23†view license†creativecommons.org L39: ### Current browse context:\nL40: \nL41: cs.DC\nL42: \nL43: cite24†< pr